## Data

### Series used (FRED)
| FRED id | Description | Native frequency |
|---------|-------------|------------------|
| MORTGAGE30US | 30-year fixed mortgage rate (target) | Weekly |
| DGS10 | 10-year Treasury yield | Daily |
| FEDFUNDS | Federal funds effective rate | Monthly |
| UNRATE | Civilian unemployment rate | Monthly |
| CPIAUCSL | CPI all urban consumers | Monthly |
| HOUST | Housing starts | Monthly |

Source: [FRED](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/) (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis).  
This project uses **public FRED graph CSV downloads** in the notebooks (no API key required for that method).  
If you use `fredapi` instead, you need a free FRED API key from https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html.

### How to get the data
1. Open `notebooks/Capstone_Preprocessing_Feature_Eng.ipynb` (or the baseline notebook).
2. Run the data-acquisition cells top to bottom. They download the series above and align them to a weekly calendar.
3. No files need to be placed in `data/` beforehand for a first run.

### Local cache
After a successful run you may save outputs:

- `data/raw/<SERIES>.csv` — individual FRED pulls  
- `data/processed/mortgage_features_weekly.csv` — aligned exogenous feature matrix used for modeling  


### Feature rule (Phase 1)
Predictors are **exogenous only**.  
Locked feature list: `src/phase1_feature_list.txt`.  
Locked model helpers: `src/phase1_locked_model.py`.  
Model card: `src/MODEL_CARD_PHASE1.md`.
